{
  "id": "contexts/fragments/02_enumerator_list",
  "topic": "contexts",
  "subtopic": "fragments",
  "title": "X-macro lists",
  "summary": "A list of macro calls compiles where its includer first expands it",
  "prose": "`errors.def` is an X-macro list: `codes.cpp` includes it once to declare the enumerators and once to name them. Opened on its own, it compiles inside the enum, so its entries show as enumerators.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "codes.cpp",
      "text": "enum class Code {\n#define ERROR(name, value) name = value,\n#include \"errors.def\"\n#undef ERROR\n};\n\nconst char* text(Code c) {\n    switch (c) {\n#define ERROR(name, value) \\\n    case Code::name: return #name;\n#include \"errors.def\"\n#undef ERROR\n    }\n    return \"\";\n}\n",
      "markers": []
    },
    {
      "path": "errors.def",
      "text": "ERROR(NotFound, 404)\nERROR(Forbidden, 403)\n",
      "markers": []
    }
  ],
